# Scrollbars — one behavior everywhere

All scrollable product surfaces use the **same hover-fade scrollbar** as Monaco (Cursor-like): thumb/track **hidden by default**, **fades in** on pointer enter or while actively scrolling, **fades out** after leave.

## Required pattern

| Surface | Implementation |
| ------- | -------------- |
| App pages, chat, history | `{ ScrollArea }` from `ui/scroll-area` — **do not** pass `type`; default is `hover` |
| Modals (About, etc.) | `ScaffyModalBody scroll` — wraps `ScrollArea` internally; **no** `type="always"` / `type="scroll"` |
| Monaco editor | `monaco-editor.css` — same `--scaffy-scrollbar-*` tokens |
| Markdown `<pre>` only | `native-scroll-x` in `scroll-area.css` (documented ADR-017 exception) |

## Do not

- Pass `type="always"`, `type="scroll"`, or `type="auto"` on product `ScrollArea` unless a new ADR documents an exception.
- Add per-page scrollbar colors, sizes, or fade overrides.
- Use native `overflow: auto` scrollbars in feature views when `ScrollArea` fits.

## Styling (single source)

- **Tokens:** `--scaffy-scrollbar-inset`, `--scaffy-scrollbar-size`, `--scaffy-scrollbar-visible-opacity`, fade durations in `scroll-area.css` (`:root`).
- **ScrollArea:** fade via `[data-state='visible']` on `[data-slot='scroll-area-scrollbar']` in `scroll-area.css`.
- **Monaco:** slider opacity tied to `.scaffy-monaco-editor:hover` / `.scrollbar.active` in `monaco-editor.css`.

## Layout

- `ScrollArea` root: `min-h-0`, flex/grid parent must constrain height (`minmax(0,1fr)` for modal lg grid — see ADR-018).
- Content padding on **inner** wrappers, not on `ScrollArea` root.

See **ADR-017** and **ADR-018** in `docs/decisions.md`.
